# Hand-authored kelp blade stamps: one folder per source, each holding a
# diffuse (sRGB, alpha carries the cutout) and, optionally, an arm and a 16-bit
# disp map — either one absent is derived from the diffuse. One whole blade or
# frond per stamp, base on the bottom edge and tip at the top, standing the way
# it is drawn. `source.json` declares lengthMetres. See
# ../../../../docs/scatter-forge/kelp.md.
#
# Large binaries, kept out of git the way /assets/ is. With no source here the
# forge generates its blades instead, so a fresh clone still builds. This rule
# keeps the file itself tracked so the folder survives that clone.
*
!.gitignore
